    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8290" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">circum-sĕco</span></b> , no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i>, sectum
				āre, v. a., <i>to cut</i> or <i>pare around</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">radices vitium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 114, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ungulas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					6, 6, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tuberculum ferro,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					7, 5, 13</span></i>
			: aliquid serrulā, <i>to saw
			around</i>, * <i><span class="en">Cic. Clu. 64, 180</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">circumsecta aluta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Scrib. Comp. 229</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To circumcise</i>, of the Jews (usu. circumcido),
				<i><span class="en">Suet. Dom. 12</span></i>.</div>
